  "Question": "If the polynomial \\(x^2 y^{|m|}-3x+1\\) is a trinomial of degree 3, find the value of \\(m\\). (If there are multiple answers, separate them with commas.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "1，-1",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": true,
  "Solution": "The degree of the highest-degree term \\(x^2 y^{|m|}\\) is \\(2+|m|\\). From \\(2+|m|=3\\), we obtain \\(|m|=1\\), so \\(m=1\\) or \\(m=-1\\).",
